          "subject": "Honor Retry-After and preserve server retry deadlines (#47641)",
          "parents": [
            "ab021e9f137c9daacf6ae06a495f3c7d6199fab2"
          ],
          "body_excerpt": "## Why\n\nHTTP retries used local backoff even when the server supplied `Retry-After`. Relative retry delays also failed to account for time spent propagating errors or reporting retries.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Parse `Retry-After` delay seconds and HTTP dates into a monotonic deadline captured when response headers arrive.\n- Honor that deadline for HTTP retries, falling back to local backoff when valid advice is absent.\n- Preserve deadlines through API and Bedrock error mapping, stream retries, and exhausted retry state. Expired advice remains a zero delay instead of triggering local backoff.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd coverage for header parsing, deadline countdown and expiry, error mapping after exhausted HTTP retries, and delayed stream retry notifications. Update Responses and remote compaction tests"
        },
